---
kind: quest
luteVersion: "0.25.0"
uses: ../world.schema.yaml
title: Unmoored
---

/*
  The frame quest. It becomes available at the first release — episode 3, where
  forty metres of ship stop being ship — because that is where "the ship is
  coming apart" stops being a warning and becomes a measurement.

  What this quest WANTED to say from the start: "and the shed is still short of
  the greenhouse when the story ends". Until dsl 0.21.0 it could not: every
  `done=` was evaluated continuously, so the hold-the-line objective
  (`run.shedPressure < 2`) was satisfied at activation and the quest completed
  before the player had done anything (T9.4). The file shipped the positive form
  instead — `aHandAtTheCoupling`, `somebodyToWalkWith` — with the losing side on
  `fail=`, and this comment said so.

  `noNewReasons` is that sentence, now written: `on="runEnd"` makes its `done`
  judged ONLY when the engine raises `runEnd` while the quest is active, never
  continuously (dsl 0.21.0 §7a.2). The quest can no longer complete mid-run; it
  completes only once a `runEnd` has found the schedule handed at most one reason,
  with the other two required objectives done.
  The two positive-form objectives stay: they were the stand-ins, but they are
  also true of the story — the completion line names both — so the quest now
  asks for all three. `fail=` stays too, and still fires the moment the shed runs
  four modules ahead. Between the two (pressure 2 or 3 at `runEnd`) the quest
  simply stays active: the run ended with reasons given, and nothing lost outright.

  `visited()` is now legal in `done=` as well (§7a.1), so T9.3's first draft —
  "arrive at the bridge", `visited('haven.s01ep10')` — is writable. It is not
  restored: the prologue has two endings, and the frame quest is about the shed,
  not which terminal the player reaches.
*/
<quest id="unmoored" title="Unmoored" start="true" fail="run.shedPressure >= 4" after="visited('haven.s01ep03')">
<objective id="aHandAtTheCoupling" title="Have somebody aboard who can stop the shed" done="count(can_halt(_)) >= 1"/>
<objective id="somebodyToWalkWith" title="Give Vesna a reason to work with you" done="run.vesnaTrust >= 1"/>
<objective id="noNewReasons" title="Give the schedule no new reasons" on="runEnd" done="run.shedPressure < 2"/>
<objective id="theOrderOnPaper" title="Get the order of release onto paper you have read" done="@vesnaHasPaper" optional/>
<on event="questComplete">
@narrator: A hand that could reach the coupling, and somebody willing to stand next to it.
</on>
<on event="questFailed">
@narrator: The schedule ran out ahead of the crew, and the ship went on subtracting itself.
</on>
</quest>
